WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
The gap: acting inside your control.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.170
Ten at night. A message from a teammate: I have not started my part. The presentation is tomorrow.

3
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:14.980
Sinta's thumbs are already typing something sharp.

4
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:21.240
But between the message and her reply there is a gap. It is about two seconds wide.

5
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:29.900
The stimulus is fixed. She did not choose it. The gap is where she chooses. And the response is entirely hers. Ownership is refusing to let the stimulus write your reply.

6
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:38.490
Her first draft: you always make me do everything. That sentence hands the pen to him. She deletes it. The second begins with I choose.

7
00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:46.850
Your language is a live diagnostic. I have to, they made me, there is nothing I can do: these are reactive tells.

8
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:55.090
I choose, I will, here is what I can do: these are ownership tells. Listen to yourself for one day, and count.

9
00:00:55.490 --> 00:01:01.470
The next morning she does one thing nobody asked for: a one-page checklist for the group's next project. That is exactly why interviewers ask for examples of it.

10
00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:08.870
The stimulus is fixed. The response is yours. Your words show who holds the pen.

11
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:13.670
Now it is your turn. Pick one frustrating moment from this week. Find the gap, and rewrite your reply.
